  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c71e7ef2-74df-4658-9a44-e9c3c913a8a2"><problem><para>
      <para>For questions 1 - 2, determine the number of solutions. Then solve the equation.</para>
      <para>\(3x^2=48\)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>0 solutions</para><para>1 solution; \(x=4\)</para><para>2 solutions; \(x=4\) and \(x=-4\)</para><para>2 solutions; \(x=12\) and \(x=-12\)</para></problem><solution><para>2 solutions; \(x=4\) and \(x=-4\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is two solutions; \(x=4\) and \(x=-4\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
